/*!
@defgroup mcm MCM Driver
@details The MCUXpresso SDK provides APIs for MCUXpresso SDK devices' Cortex-M85 MCM operation.

The Cortex-M85 MCM (CM85_MCM) is a miscellaneous control module connected onto
the Cortex-M85 PPB bus. It exposes the FPU exception interrupt enables and
status flags, the TCM write-abort detection, and a debugger-readable view of
the CM85 fault registers and the current program counter.

The MCM driver supports:
  - Enabling and disabling the per-source interrupts in ISCR: TCM write abort
    plus the six FPU exceptions (invalid operation, divide-by-zero, overflow,
    underflow, inexact, input denormal)
  - Reading the asserted ISCR status flags
  - Clearing the TCM write-abort status (the FPU status bits mirror FPSCR and
    must be cleared via FPSCR)
  - Reading the raw and decoded process-fault state from PFSHR + PFSLR (MMFSR,
    BFSR, UFSR, SFSR and the three HFSR bits)
  - Reading the current program counter (CURRPC)

*/
